Sentinel Forge Study Workstation
Version: v12 · Date: 2026-09-13
Repository: study-workstation-web
Status: Active development — practice twin

Overview
The Sentinel Forge Study Workstation is a browser-based study tool built for university students. It combines a spatial index board, a flashcard library, a retrieval-practice engine, an AI assistant, and a structured study-session tracker — all in a single self-contained HTML file that runs offline with no server required.
Data persists in browser localStorage (key: gridindex-v1). A JSON export/import bridge allows cards to move between this web version and a companion Grok copy. The two instances do not share a database.
The Retrieve tab implements the retrieve stage of RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation): keyword scoring without embeddings or vector search. This makes the architecture transparent and teachable at the undergraduate level.

