Why This Dashboard Is Designed This Way
Neural-Inclusive Design Rationale
This workstation was deliberately designed to serve students with a range of cognitive and sensory profiles. The design is not a retrofit — it is the foundation. The architecture follows Shannon's Neural Lattice Cognitive Architecture (v1.0), which applies zone-based cognitive load management, structured protocol layers, and neurodivergent-optimized information chunking to AI-human collaboration tools.
The following profiles were considered during design:
Profile
Design consideration implemented
ADHD
Short chunked content fields; Pomodoro-aligned session tab; minimal visual clutter
Dyslexia
BDA Dyslexia Style Guide 2023 font/spacing/tint guidance; left-aligned text; generous line height
Dysgraphia
Template-driven card creation; AI-assisted card generation on request
Dyscalculia
Alphanumeric board coordinates (A1, B3) rather than pure number grids; row and column labels always visible
Autism
Predictable, consistent layout; no auto-playing elements; explicit state feedback on every action
Anxiety / PTSD
Low-stimulation dark theme; no timed pressure outside student-controlled sessions
Low vision
High-contrast dark tokens; scalable text; no information conveyed by colour alone
Deaf / Hard of hearing
No audio dependency; all information is visual
Stress-related memory disorders
Spatial index board externalises working memory load; retrieval practice reduces cramming pressure


